{"id":"word:hebrew:H4347","type":"word","title":"מַכָּה","subtitle":"H4347 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a blow (in 2 Chronicles 2:10, of the flail); by implication, a wound ; figuratively, carnage , also pestilence","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מַכָּה (H4347) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 48 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מַכָּה (makkâh) means a blow (in 2 Chronicles 2:10, of the flail); by implication, a wound ; figuratively, carnage , also pestilence First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 20 21."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מַכָּה","transliteration":"makkâh","pronunciation":"mak-kaw'","strong":"H4347","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4347","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["מַכָּ֖ה","מַכָּ֣ה","מַכָּ֥ה","הַ/מַּכִּים֙","הַ/מַּכָּ֖ה"],"morphs":[["HNcfsa",17],["HTd/Ncfpa",4],["HNcfpc/Sp3fs",4],["HTd/Ncfsa",3],["HNcfsc",3],["HNcfpa",2],["HNcfpc",2],["HC/Ncfsa",2],["HNcfpc/Sp2ms",1],["HR/Ncfsc",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a blow (in 2 Chronicles 2:10, of the flail); by implication, a wound ; figuratively, carnage , also pestilence","usage":"beaten, blow, plague, slaughter, smote, × sore, stripe, stroke, wound(-ed).","full":"H4347. makkah or makkeh מַכָּה noun feminine blow, wound, slaughter ; — absolute ׳מ 1Sam 4:8 +; construct מַכַּת Isa 10:26 +; suffix מַכָּתִי Jer 10:19 ; 15:18 , etc.; **plural מַכִּי֥֥ 2Kin 8:29 = 9:15 2Chr 22:6 ; מַכּוֺת absolute Zech 13:6 +, construct,' etc.; plural מַכּוֺת absolute 2Kin 8:29 +; construct Deut 29:21 +; suffix מַכֹּתְךָ 28:59 , מַכּוֺתַיִךְ Jer 30:17 , etc.; &#8212; 1. a. blow, stripe , literally of scourging, chastising Deut 25:3 ; Prov 20:30 (|| מֶּצַע חַבֻּרוֺת ); חֶרֶב מַכַּת Est 9:5 (as accusative of congnate meaning with verb). b. beating, scourging , figurative of defeat of Midian Isa 10:26 (|| שׁוֺט עוֺרֵר ). c. often wound 1Kin 22:35 ; 2Kin 8:29 ; 9:15 2Chr 22:6 (read ׳מִןהַֿמּ ), Zech 13:6 ( יָדֶיךָ בֵּין ); symbolic of violence Jer 6:7 (+ חֳלִי ); טְרִיָּה וּמַכָּה וְחַבּוּרָה מֶּצַע Isa 1:6 (of Judah, under figure of maltreated man), compare Micah 1:9 אֲנוּשָׁה׳מ ), Nahum 3:19 (|| שֶׁבֶר ; of Nineveh), especially in Jeremiah (of Judah): Jer 10:19 ; 14:17 ; 30:12 (all + נַחֲלָה severe ; || שֶׁבֶר ), 15:18 ( ׳מ אֲנוּשָׁה ), 19:8 ; Jeremiah 47:17; 50:13 , as accusative of congnate meaning with verb 30:14 , with verb רָפָא heal 30:17 ; also מ ׳מַחַץ Isa 30:26 (|| שֶׁבֶר ); of wounds made by ׳י s arrows Psa 64:8 . 2 = slaughter 1Sam 4:10 ; 14:30 , usually as accusative of congnate meaning with verb with הִכָּה Josh 10:20 ; 1Sam 6:19 ; 14:14 ; 19:8 ; 23:5 ; 1Kin 20:21 ; 2Chr 13:17 . 3 = defeat , as accusative of congnate meaning with verb with הִכָּה Josh 10:10 ; Joshua 11:33; 15:8 ; 2Chr 28:5 ; = conquest (of ׳י ) Isa 14:6 . 4 plague , especially disease, as punishment (of ׳י ), 1Sam 4:8 ; Deut 28:59 (3 t. in verse) (|| חֳלִי ), 28:61 (|| id. ), 29:21 (|| תַּחֲלֻאִים ), Lev 26:21 (H), as accusative of congnate meaning with verb Num 11:33 . &#8212; מַכּוֺת 2Chr 2:9 read מַכֹּלֶת (see אכל ) as || 1 Kings 5:25, so ᵑ9 ᵐ5 Be Öttli and Th 1Ki 5:25 .","rootNote":"or (masculine) מַכֶּה ; (plural only) from 5221 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 20 21","keyReferences":["1Kgs 20 21","1Kgs 22 35","1Sam 4 8","1Sam 4 10","1Sam 6 19","1Sam 14 14","1Sam 14 30","1Sam 19 8"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":48,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 20 21","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מַכָּ֥ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 35","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":35,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/מַּכָּ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 4 8","book":"1Sam","chapter":4,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מַכָּ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HN